1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,766
One morning in 1066, a battle in England changed the words you speak today.

2
00:00:06,966 --> 00:00:11,384
On the fourteenth of October, the Norman knights charged up the hill at Hastings.

3
00:00:11,384 --> 00:00:15,366
By evening, King Harold was dead, and England had a French speaking king.

4
00:00:16,566 --> 00:00:20,377
For three hundred years, the rulers spoke French.

5
00:00:20,377 --> 00:00:23,955
Thousands of French words poured into English.

6
00:00:23,955 --> 00:00:30,333
Then, slowly, English came back, to the courts in 1362, and to the throne in 1399.

7
00:00:31,533 --> 00:00:35,812
That is why we say cow and pig for the animal, but beef and pork for the meat.

8
00:00:35,812 --> 00:00:37,238
The farmers spoke English.

9
00:00:37,238 --> 00:00:38,500
The lords spoke French.

